        "label": "Friction loss depends on the length and size of the pipework: a longer pipe or a smaller bore always loses more at the same flow",
        "ok": true,
        "source": "https://www.atlascopco.com/en-us/construction-equipment/resources/dewatering-pumps-guide/pump-head"
      },
      {
        "label": "In turbulent flow the resistance is proportional to the square of the mean flow velocity: twice the flow gives four times the friction head, in every bore and length",
